{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"language":"python","display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":19588835}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# U.S. Presidential and Senate Election Analysis (1976–2020)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"This project analyzes U.S. Presidential and Senate election data from 1976 to 2020. The data was cleaned by handling missing values, correcting data types, checking for duplicates and invalid records, and fixing Senate runoff results. The analysis then looks at national presidential vote share, Senate seat share, split ticket voting, and presidential winning margins to understand how election results changed over time.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Data Cleaning**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\npath = \"/kaggle/input/datasets/manishamali/us-election-analysis-dataset/\"\npres_raw = pd.read_csv(path + \"1976-2020-president.csv\", encoding=\"latin-1\")\nsen_raw = pd.read_csv(path + \"1976-2020-senate.csv\", encoding=\"latin-1\")\n\nprint(\"President data:\", pres_raw.shape)\nprint(\"Senate data:\", sen_raw.shape)\n\nprint(pres_raw.isnull().sum())\nprint(sen_raw.isnull().sum())\nprint(\"Duplicates:\", pres_raw.duplicated().sum(), sen_raw.duplicated().sum())\n\n\ndef clean(df):\n    df.columns = df.columns.str.strip().str.lower().str.replace(\" \", \"_\")\n\n    for col in df.select_dtypes(include=\"object\"):\n        df[col] = df[col].map(lambda x: x.strip() if isinstance(x, str) else x)\n        df[col] = df[col].replace(\"\", pd.NA)\n\n    num_cols = [\"year\", \"state_fips\", \"state_cen\", \"state_ic\", \"candidatevotes\", \"totalvotes\"]\n    for col in num_cols:\n        df[col] = pd.to_numeric(df[col], errors=\"coerce\").astype(\"Int64\")\n\n    return df\n\n\npres = clean(pres_raw.copy())\nsen = clean(sen_raw.copy())\n\npres = pres.drop(columns=\"notes\")\n\npres[\"writein\"] = pres[\"writein\"].astype(\"boolean\").fillna(False)\nfor col in [\"writein\", \"special\", \"unofficial\"]:\n    sen[col] = sen[col].astype(\"boolean\")\n\nprint(pres.loc[pres[\"candidate\"].isna(), \"party_simplified\"].value_counts())\nprint(sen.loc[sen[\"candidate\"].isna(), \"party_simplified\"].value_counts())\n\npres[\"party_detailed\"] = pres[\"party_detailed\"].fillna(pres[\"party_simplified\"])\nsen[\"party_detailed\"] = sen[\"party_detailed\"].fillna(sen[\"party_simplified\"])\n\nadmin_labels = [\"OTHER\", \"SCATTER\", \"SCATTERED\", \"UNDER VOTE\", \"UNDER VOTES\",\n                \"OVER VOTE\", \"OVER VOTES\", \"BLANK VOTE\", \"BLANK VOTES\"]\n\nfor df in [pres, sen]:\n    df[\"admin_vote\"] = df[\"candidate\"].isna() | df[\"candidate\"].str.upper().isin(admin_labels)\n\n# Georgia's 2020 runoffs were held in January 2021, so count them as 2020\nsen[\"stage\"] = sen[\"stage\"].str.lower()\nsen.loc[(sen[\"year\"] == 2021) & (sen[\"stage\"] == \"runoff\"), \"year\"] = 2020\n\npres = pres[pres[\"year\"].between(1976, 2020)].copy()\nsen = sen[sen[\"year\"].between(1976, 2020)].copy()\n\n# only general elections and runoffs\nsen = sen[sen[\"stage\"].isin([\"gen\", \"runoff\"])]\n\n# if a race went to a runoff, the runoff decides the winner\nrace = [\"year\", \"state\", \"special\"]\nhas_runoff = sen.groupby(race)[\"stage\"].transform(lambda s: (s == \"runoff\").any())\nsen = sen[~has_runoff | (sen[\"stage\"] == \"runoff\")].copy()\n\nwy = (sen[\"state\"] == \"WYOMING\") & (sen[\"year\"] == 2020)\nsen.loc[wy & (sen[\"candidate\"] == \"CYNTHIA M. LUMMIS\"), \"party_simplified\"] = \"REPUBLICAN\"\nsen.loc[wy & (sen[\"candidate\"] == \"MERAV BEN DAVID\"), \"party_simplified\"] = \"DEMOCRAT\"\n\nprint(sen[\"mode\"].value_counts())\nprint(sen[\"unofficial\"].value_counts())\n\n# remove invalid vote counts\npres = pres[(pres[\"candidatevotes\"] >= 0) & (pres[\"totalvotes\"] > 0)]\nsen = sen[(sen[\"candidatevotes\"] >= 0) & (sen[\"totalvotes\"] > 0)]\n\nprint(\"Votes above total (pres):\", (pres[\"candidatevotes\"] > pres[\"totalvotes\"]).sum())\nprint(\"Votes above total (sen):\", (sen[\"candidatevotes\"] > sen[\"totalvotes\"]).sum())\n\npres = pres.drop_duplicates().copy()\nsen = sen.drop_duplicates().copy()\n\n# candidate votes should add up to the total in each race\npres_check = pres.groupby([\"year\", \"state\"]).agg(\n    cand=(\"candidatevotes\", \"sum\"), total=(\"totalvotes\", \"first\"))\nsen_check = sen.groupby(race + [\"stage\"]).agg(\n    cand=(\"candidatevotes\", \"sum\"), total=(\"totalvotes\", \"first\"))\n\nprint(\"Pres total mismatches:\", (pres_check[\"cand\"] != pres_check[\"total\"]).sum())\nprint(\"Senate total mismatches:\", (sen_check[\"cand\"] != sen_check[\"total\"]).sum())\n\nprint(\"Final shapes:\", pres.shape, sen.shape)\nprint(pres.isnull().sum())\nprint(sen.isnull().sum())\nprint(pres.dtypes)\nprint(sen.dtypes)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-21T20:10:14.103846Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-21T20:10:14.104147Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.019597Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-21T20:10:14.104116Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.018583Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"President data: (4287, 15)\nSenate data: (3629, 19)\nyear                   0\nstate                  0\nstate_po               0\nstate_fips             0\nstate_cen              0\nstate_ic               0\noffice                 0\ncandidate            287\nparty_detailed       456\nwritein                3\ncandidatevotes         0\ntotalvotes             0\nversion                0\nnotes               4287\nparty_simplified       0\ndtype: int64\nyear                  0\nstate                 0\nstate_po              0\nstate_fips            0\nstate_cen             0\nstate_ic              0\noffice                0\ndistrict              0\nstage                 0\nspecial               0\ncandidate           423\nparty_detailed      599\nwritein               0\nmode                  0\ncandidatevotes        0\ntotalvotes            0\nunofficial            0\nversion               0\nparty_simplified      0\ndtype: int64\nDuplicates: 0 0\nparty_simplified\nOTHER          285\nLIBERTARIAN      1\nDEMOCRAT         1\nName: count, dtype: int64\nparty_simplified\nOTHER    423\nName: count, dtype: int64\nmode\ntotal    3597\nName: count, dtype: int64\nunofficial\nFalse    3588\nTrue        9\nName: count, dtype: Int64\nVotes above total (pres): 0\nVotes above total (sen): 0\nPres total mismatches: 0\nSenate total mismatches: 0\nFinal shapes: (4287, 15) (3597, 20)\nyear                  0\nstate                 0\nstate_po              0\nstate_fips            0\nstate_cen             0\nstate_ic              0\noffice                0\ncandidate           287\nparty_detailed        0\nwritein               0\ncandidatevotes        0\ntotalvotes            0\nversion               0\nparty_simplified      0\nadmin_vote            0\ndtype: int64\nyear                  0\nstate                 0\nstate_po              0\nstate_fips            0\nstate_cen             0\nstate_ic              0\noffice                0\ndistrict              0\nstage                 0\nspecial               0\ncandidate           420\nparty_detailed        0\nwritein               0\nmode                  0\ncandidatevotes        0\ntotalvotes            0\nunofficial            0\nversion               0\nparty_simplified      0\nadmin_vote            0\ndtype: int64\nyear                  Int64\nstate                object\nstate_po             object\nstate_fips            Int64\nstate_cen             Int64\nstate_ic              Int64\noffice               object\ncandidate            object\nparty_detailed       object\nwritein             boolean\ncandidatevotes        Int64\ntotalvotes            Int64\nversion               int64\nparty_simplified     object\nadmin_vote             bool\ndtype: object\nyear                  Int64\nstate                object\nstate_po             object\nstate_fips            Int64\nstate_cen             Int64\nstate_ic              Int64\noffice               object\ndistrict             object\nstage                object\nspecial             boolean\ncandidate            object\nparty_detailed       object\nwritein             boolean\nmode                 object\ncandidatevotes        Int64\ntotalvotes            Int64\nunofficial          boolean\nversion               int64\nparty_simplified     object\nadmin_vote             bool\ndtype: object\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*The data was checked for missing values, duplicates, wrong data types and invalid vote counts. No duplicate rows were found and no rows were dropped because of missing values. The empty notes column was removed, missing party_detailed values were filled from party_simplified, and the 3 missing writein values were set to False. Rows with no candidate name are grouped “other” votes, so they were kept and flagged. 32 Senate rows were removed, all Georgia first round results from 1992, 2008 and 2020, because those races were decided by a runoff. Georgia’s January 2021 runoffs were counted as 2020, and the Wyoming 2020 party labels were corrected.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Number of Senate races per year**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Number of Senate races per year\nraces_per_cycle = sen.drop_duplicates(\n    [\"year\", \"state\", \"special\"]\n).groupby(\"year\").size()\n\nprint(races_per_cycle)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.021594Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.022061Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.034553Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.022025Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.03374Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"year\n1976    33\n1978    35\n1980    33\n1982    33\n1984    33\n1986    34\n1988    33\n1990    35\n1992    35\n1994    35\n1996    34\n1998    34\n2000    34\n2002    34\n2004    34\n2006    33\n2008    35\n2010    37\n2012    33\n2014    36\n2016    34\n2018    35\n2020    35\ndtype: int64\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*The number of Senate races ranges from 33 to 37 per year. Normally about 33 or 34 seats are up in each cycle, and years like 2010 (37 races) and 2014 (36 races) are higher because of special elections.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**National Presidential Vote Share by Party (1976–2020)**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"votes = pres.groupby([\"year\", \"party_simplified\"])[\"candidatevotes\"].sum().unstack(fill_value=0)\n\nvote_share = votes.div(votes.sum(axis=1), axis=0) * 100\n\nprint(vote_share.round(1))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.035631Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.036057Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.104111Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.036023Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.103134Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"party_simplified  DEMOCRAT  LIBERTARIAN  OTHER  REPUBLICAN\nyear                                                      \n1976                  49.9          0.1    2.4        47.6\n1980                  41.0          1.0    7.5        50.5\n1984                  40.4          0.2    0.9        58.5\n1988                  45.5          0.4    0.9        53.1\n1992                  42.9          0.3   19.8        37.1\n1996                  49.1          0.5   10.0        40.5\n2000                  48.1          0.4    3.9        47.6\n2004                  48.1          0.3    1.0        50.6\n2008                  52.8          0.4    1.5        45.4\n2012                  50.9          0.9    1.2        47.0\n2016                  48.0          3.0    3.1        45.8\n2020                  51.3          1.1    0.8        46.8\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*The Democratic and Republican parties received the largest share of votes in most elections. Republican vote share was highest in 1984 at 58.5%, while Democratic vote share was highest in 2008 at 52.8%. The 1992 election had a relatively high share of votes for other parties at 19.8%.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Presidential Vote Share by Year**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"share = vote_share[[\"DEMOCRAT\", \"REPUBLICAN\"]].copy()\nshare.columns = [\"Democrat\", \"Republican\"]\n\nshare.plot(kind=\"bar\", figsize=(10, 5))\n\nplt.title(\"Presidential Vote Share by Year\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Year\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Vote Share (%)\")\nplt.xticks(rotation=45)\nplt.legend()\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.105167Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.105464Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.587691Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.105436Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.586752Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":4},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*The chart shows that Democratic and Republican vote shares changed across election years. Republicans had a higher vote share in 1980, 1984, 1988, and 2004, while Democrats had a higher share in several other years. The largest Republican share was in 1984 (58.5%), while the highest Democratic share was in 2008 (52.8%). In 2000, the two parties had very similar vote shares.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Split Ticket Voting by Year**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Find the presidential winner for each state and year\npres_winner = pres.loc[pres.groupby([\"year\", \"state\"])[\"candidatevotes\"].idxmax(),\n    [\"year\", \"state\", \"party_simplified\", \"candidate\"]]\n\npres_winner.columns = [\"year\", \"state\", \"pres_party\", \"pres_candidate\"]\n\n# Find the Senate winner for each state and year\nsen_winner = sen.loc[sen.groupby([\"year\", \"state\", \"special\"])[\"candidatevotes\"].idxmax(),\n    [\"year\", \"state\", \"special\", \"party_simplified\", \"candidate\"]]\n\nsen_winner.columns = [\"year\", \"state\", \"special\", \"sen_party\", \"sen_candidate\"]\n\n# Compare presidential and Senate winners\nresult = sen_winner.merge(pres_winner,on=[\"year\", \"state\"])\n\nresult[\"different_party\"] = (result[\"pres_party\"] != result[\"sen_party\"])\n\n# Calculate the percentage of split-ticket results by year\nsplit_rate = (result.groupby(\"year\")[\"different_party\"].mean() * 100)\nprint(split_rate.round(1))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.59021Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.590635Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.629423Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.590592Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.62842Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"year\n1976    42.4\n1980    39.4\n1984    54.5\n1988    51.5\n1992    31.4\n1996    29.4\n2000    29.4\n2004    20.6\n2008    20.0\n2012    24.2\n2016     0.0\n2020     2.9\nName: different_party, dtype: float64\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":5},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*Split ticket voting was relatively high in earlier election years, with the highest level in 1984 at 54.5%. It gradually decreased over time and reached 0% in 2016. In 2020, the rate was only 2.9%, showing that presidential and Senate winners were from different parties much less often in the later years.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n\nplt.bar(split_rate.index.astype(str), split_rate)\n\nplt.title(\"Split Ticket Voting by Year\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Year\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Split Ticket (%)\")\nplt.xticks(rotation=45)\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.630634Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.630962Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.847107Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.630934Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.846195Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":6},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Median Winning Margin in Presidential Elections**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"results = []\n\nfor (year, state), data in pres.groupby([\"year\", \"state\"]):\n    data = data[~data[\"admin_vote\"]].sort_values(\"candidatevotes\", ascending=False)\n\n    if len(data) >= 2:\n        winner = data.iloc[0]\n        second = data.iloc[1]\n        margin = (winner[\"candidatevotes\"] - second[\"candidatevotes\"]) / winner[\"totalvotes\"]\n\n        results.append([year, state, winner[\"candidate\"], winner[\"party_simplified\"],\n                        second[\"candidate\"], margin])\n\nmargins = pd.DataFrame(results, columns=[\"year\", \"state\", \"winner\", \"party\",\n                                         \"runner_up\", \"margin\"])\n\nyear_margin = margins.groupby(\"year\")[\"margin\"].agg([\"median\", \"min\", \"max\"])\nprint((year_margin * 100).round(1))\n\nprint(\"\\nClosest races:\")\nprint(margins.nsmallest(5, \"margin\"))\n\n# DC is left out since it is always one sided\nprint(\"\\nLargest margins:\")\nprint(margins[margins[\"state\"] != \"DISTRICT OF COLUMBIA\"].nlargest(5, \"margin\"))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.848643Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.849019Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-21T20:10:18.620436Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-21T20:10:17.848987Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-21T20:10:18.619549Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"      median  min   max\nyear                   \n1976     6.1  0.2  65.1\n1980    10.6  0.2  61.5\n1984    22.1  0.2  71.7\n1988    11.7  1.6  68.3\n1992     8.2  0.6  75.5\n1996    10.3  1.0  75.9\n2000    12.8  0.0  76.2\n2004    12.9  0.4  79.8\n2008    15.1  0.1  85.9\n2012    16.9  0.9  83.6\n2016    17.1  0.2  86.4\n2020    16.5  0.2  86.8\n\nClosest races:\n     year          state           winner       party         runner_up  \\\n315  2000        FLORIDA  BUSH, GEORGE W.  REPUBLICAN          GORE, AL   \n337  2000     NEW MEXICO         GORE, AL    DEMOCRAT   BUSH, GEORGE W.   \n433  2008       MISSOURI     MCCAIN, JOHN  REPUBLICAN  OBAMA, BARACK H.   \n72   1980  MASSACHUSETTS   REAGAN, RONALD  REPUBLICAN     CARTER, JIMMY   \n37   1976         OREGON     FORD, GERALD  REPUBLICAN     CARTER, JIMMY   \n\n       margin  \n315  0.000090  \n337  0.000611  \n433  0.001334  \n72   0.001517  \n37   0.001663  \n\nLargest margins:\n     year    state            winner       party         runner_up    margin\n95   1980     UTAH    REAGAN, RONALD  REPUBLICAN     CARTER, JIMMY  0.522089\n146  1984     UTAH    REAGAN, RONALD  REPUBLICAN   MONDALE, WALTER  0.498266\n503  2012     UTAH      ROMNEY, MITT  REPUBLICAN  OBAMA, BARACK H.  0.480409\n114  1984    IDAHO    REAGAN, RONALD  REPUBLICAN   MONDALE, WALTER  0.459725\n560  2016  WYOMING  TRUMP, DONALD J.  REPUBLICAN  CLINTON, HILLARY  0.457695\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":7},{"cell_type":"code","source":"plt.figure(figsize=(9, 5))\n\nplt.plot(\n    year_margin.index,\n    year_margin[\"median\"] * 100,\n    marker=\"o\"\n)\n\nplt.title(\"Median Presidential Winning Margin\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Year\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Winning Margin (%)\")\n\nplt.xticks(rotation=45)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-21T20:10:18.621822Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-21T20:10:18.622191Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-21T20:10:18.837129Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-21T20:10:18.622149Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-21T20:10:18.836229Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 900x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":8},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*The median winning margin was lowest in 1976 at about 6% and highest in 1984 at about 22%, the year of Reagan’s landslide. After a dip to 8.2% in 1992, it rose steadily to 17.1% in 2016 and stayed close to that in 2020 at 16.5%. This means the typical state has become much less competitive over time. The closest race in the data is Florida in 2000, decided by less than 0.01%.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Senate Seat Share by Party**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Find the Senate winner in each state and year\nsen_winner = sen.loc[\n    sen.groupby([\"year\", \"state\", \"special\"])[\"candidatevotes\"].idxmax()]\n\n# Keep useful columns\nsen_winner = sen_winner[[\"year\", \"state\", \"special\", \"party_simplified\", \"candidate\"]]\n\n# Count seats by party\nseats = sen_winner.groupby([\"year\", \"party_simplified\"]).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n\n# Calculate seat percentage\nseat_share = seats.div(seats.sum(axis=1), axis=0) * 100\n\nprint(seats)\nprint(seat_share.round(1))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-21T20:10:18.838097Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-21T20:10:18.838336Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-21T20:10:18.86668Z","shell.execute_rep